=== OLS vs lasso CO_Mega model, ribonn TE, HCT ===

[1] Coefficients
  lasso alpha (10-fold CV, standardized predictors) = 0.00142
  lasso keeps 60 of 61 codons; sets 1 to exactly 0: CAG
  of those 1, 0 are nominally significant (p < 0.05) in the OLS model; OLS has 0 nominally significant codons overall, 0 of them kept by the lasso
  OLS vs lasso coefficients: Pearson r = 0.9994, Spearman rho = 0.9994; slope of lasso on OLS among kept codons = 0.978 (shrinkage)
  coefficient mean / SD across the 61 codons: OLS -9.577 / 5.533, lasso +0.241 / 5.414
  NOTE: the 61 sense-codon frequencies of a gene sum to ~1 (see [2]), so together with the intercept the OLS
  coefficients are only identified up to a common shift (add c to every coefficient, subtract c from the
  intercept): the huge OLS intercept / mean coefficient are that arbitrary shift, not an effect. Only the
  differences between codons (SD, correlations, slope above, all shift-invariant) are meaningful; the lasso
  penalty picks the sparse solution, which is why its intercept and mean coefficient stay small.
  intercept: OLS 9.6351, lasso -0.1846

